          "analysis": "This is an ARM-based Linux worm. It exhibits multiple malicious behaviors, including worm-like propagation by performing SSDP M-SEARCH scans on the local network (255.255.255.255:1900) to find vulnerable devices. It aggressively enumerates processes via the `/proc` filesystem and kills competing processes, particularly those involving `wget`, `curl`, `tftp`, and `ftpget`, by sending `SIGKILL`. The sample also employs stealth by detaching from the terminal (`setsid`) and changing its process name (`prctl`).",
